  "plan": {
    "goal": "Size the PLINK binary .bed storage for a GWAS genotype dataset of 14250 samples and 7433293 variants, including per-chromosome file sizing.",
    "rationale": "PLINK binary .bed packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples/byte). Total .bed size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome .bed size uses the same rule applied to one chromosome's variant count (largest chromosome = 1083490 variants). The number of per-chromosome files is the number of chromosomes; for a standard human GWAS this is 25 (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT).",
